lets exhaled by  infected people but also via smaller  aerosols  that's because the means by which a  pathogen is transmitted can be a really  complex thing to prove  especially when it infects others by  hanging suspended in the air  but a lot of the evidence we have can't  really be explained any other way and  and studies have now made it the theory  that most experts agree on  when it comes to saris kobe 2 that that  it's transmitted from infected people to  others via droplets and smaller aerosols  mostly indoors in poorly ventilated  rooms especially if those rooms are  crowded and people spend long periods of  time there  what we know about transmission in the  coronavirus that causes sars is a lot  more limited because only around eight  and a half thousand people have ever had  it and all of them were infected  almost 20 years ago but but experts  think it's more difficult to transmit  the cdc says  that the sars coronavirus spreads mostly  only through  larger respiratory droplets  during closer personal contact either  directly  or via surfaces  contaminated by those droplets  that  and another major factor that that  sufferers are mostly infectious only  when they have the full-blown symptoms  of the disease  that helped authorities get sars under  control  through strict quarantines  when it comes to mers  we know even less about transmission  than we do with sars because even fewer  people have contracted it which means  even fewer opportunities for study but  but it's believed that people can catch  it directly from animals and and camels  are a prime culprit a human to human  spread is also possible through close  contact but  as far as i can tell  no one has yet identified the exact  mechanisms of that spread  [Music]  thanks for watching stay safe and see  you again soon  [Music]  you

